## The six stages, drawn as text. A stage is a row of chunks; a chunk is [ground row, rows of text]. The last row of text is the ground itself ('#' rock, 'I' ice, '.' a pit) and is filled down to the bottom of the stage; the rows above it are the air over it, lowest last.
##
## In the air rows: '#' rock, 'I' ice, '=' ledge, 'x' crumbling slab, '^' spikes, 'h' 'H' sideways platforms (opposite phases), 'u' 'U' platforms that sink and rise, 'o' glow moth, 'f' oil flask, 'r' resin, 'w' spare wick, 'b' herding bell, 'c' cinderling, 'v' sootwing, 's' vent crab, 'k' rime beetle, 'd' driftwisp, 'j' shardling, 'g' geyser, 'i' icicle, 'm' cinder-fall zone, 'L' lamp post (checkpoint), 'G' the beacon that ends the stage.

